.TH RAMCTL 8
.SH NAME
ramctl \- configure RAM block devices
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ramctl create
.I special
.B size=value
[
.B backing=value
] [
.B compression
]
.br
.B ramctl destroy
.I special
.br
.B ramctl status
.I special
.br
.B ramctl list
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ramctl
creates and removes runtime RAM block devices.  The
.B size
argument is the visible block-device size.  The
.B backing
argument is the physical RAM budget.  Values accept K, M, and G suffixes;
.B all
selects the complete platform-reserved pool and
.I Nx
multiplies the backing size.
.PP
Without compression the visible size must equal the backing size.  With
.B compression
the visible size may exceed the physical backing, for example:
.PP
.RS
ramctl create /dev/ram1 backing=4M size=8M compression
.RE
.PP
The resulting ordinary block device may be formatted as a filesystem or as
swap.  It must be unmounted and removed from swap before it can be destroyed.
.PP
.B ramctl list
prints every currently configured RAM block device.  Devices registered by
the platform but not yet configured are omitted.
